      <ExpenseAmt>2956925</ExpenseAmt>
      <Desc>RESEARCH PROGRAMS FAR.AI CONDUCTS TECHNICAL RESEARCH TO ADDRESS FUNDAMENTAL ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE AI SAFETY CHALLENGES. IN 2024 WE PUBLISHED 12 RESEARCH PAPERS WITH ACCEPTANCES AT LEADING VENUES SUCH AS THE INTERNATIONAL CONFERENCE ON LEARNING REPRESENTATIONS ICLR, THE INTERNATIONAL CONFERENCE ON MACHINE LEARNING ICML, AND THE NEURAL INFORMATION PROCESSING SYSTEMS CONFERENCE NEURIPS. WE PARTNERED WITH GOVERNMENT-LED AI SECURITY INITIATIVES AND CONDUCTED RED-TEAMING ENGAGEMENTS ON FRONTIER AI SYSTEMS. WE ALSO SUPPORTED EXTERNAL RESEARCHERS THROUGH COLLABORATIONS, MENTORSHIPS, AND/OR OPERATIONAL SUPPORT.</Desc>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
        <ExpenseAmt>1142509</ExpenseAmt>
        <Desc>RESEARCH HUB AND COWORKING SPACE FAR.AI OPERATED A COLLABORATIVE RESEARCH HUB IN BERKELEY, PROVIDING A DEDICATED COWORKING SPACE AND IN PERSON PROGRAMS FOR RESEARCHERS AND ORGANIZATIONS WORKING ON CORE AI SECURITY, SAFETY AND GOVERNANCE CHALLENGES. HOSTING 40 TO 50 MEMBERS, THE HUB FACILITATED KNOWLEDGE EXCHANGE THROUGH WEEKLY SEMINARS WHERE RESEARCHERS AND FOUNDERS PRESENTED THEIR WORK TO THE COMMUNITY AND RAN A TEAM-IN-RESIDENCE PROGRAM DESIGNED TO SUPPORT NEW ORGANIZATIONS IN THIS FIELD.</Desc>
      </ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActy3Grp>
        <ExpenseAmt>1957949</ExpenseAmt>
        <Desc>EVENTS AND WORKSHOPS FAR.AI HOSTED AND FACILITATED TECHNICAL WORKSHOPS, MULTI-DAY CONVENINGS, AND COORDINATION EVENTS IN 2024. THESE INCLUDED LARGE-SCALE ALIGNMENT WORKSHOPS IN THE BAY AREA AND EUROPE, AS WELL AS SMALLER SPECIALIZED SESSIONS WITH RESEARCHERS, PRACTITIONERS, INDUSTRY PARTNERS, AND POLICYMAKERS. THESE EVENTS SUPPORTED COLLABORATION ON KEY TECHNICAL AND GOVERNANCE CHALLENGES IN CURRENT AND EMERGING AI SYSTEMS.</Desc>
      </ProgSrvcAccomActy3Grp>
